The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
err = pci_remap_iospace(res, iobase);
```
```c
if (err) {
    dev_warn(dev, "error %d: failed to map resource %pR\n", err, res);
    resource_list_destroy_entry(win);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `pci_remap_iospace()` is called to remap I/O space without ensuring that it can be undone if the driver's probe fails (specifically when `devm_phy_optional_get()` returns -EPROBE_DEFER). This results in attempts to remap already remapped pages, leading to a kernel crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
err = devm_pci_remap_iospace(dev, res, iobase);
```
Reason:
The new managed API `devm_pci_remap_iospace()` automatically handles the cleanup of the remapping when the driver is detached or fails, preventing the memory leak and subsequent crash that occurs from trying to remap already remapped pages.

